{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-explanation-of-vote-on-the-draft-resolution-on-eritrea","content_id":"b89c55c7-95ff-40a0-9908-6c139efcfa83","description":"UK Explanation of Vote on the draft resolution on the human rights situation in Eritrea. Delivered by UK Human Rights Ambassador, Eleanor Sanders.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>Mr President,</p>\n\n<p>The UK remains concerned by the human rights situation in Eritrea. The system of indefinite national service has a suffocating impact on the lives of Eritreans, especially young people, and has contributed to mass emigration including to the UK. It requires urgent reform.  </p>\n\n<p>We welcome areas of progress that have been made in Eritrea; including relating to essential health services and education. In particular, and as recognised in this draft resolution, we are pleased to see the release of some arbitrarily detained persons held for political or religious reasons. We encourage the Eritrean government to extend these releases to the many more that remain arbitrarily detained. </p>\n\n<p>It is clear that the Special Rapporteur’s efforts to report on the human rights situation in Eritrea continues to be needed. As such, the UK supports the draft resolution on the human rights situation in Eritrea and its outcome to extend the mandate of the Special Rapporteur.</p>\n\n<p>We thank the core group behind this resolution for  constructive and transparent engagement with the Council and support the adoption of this resolution by consensus.</p>\n\n<p>If a vote is called, we will vote YES and encourage others to do the same.</p>\n\n<p>Thank you.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-07T08:51:04Z"}],"delivered_on":"2026-07-06T00:00:00+01:00","first_public_at":"2026-07-07T09:51:04.000+01:00","image":{"alt_text":"Read ‘UN Human Rights Council 62: UK Explanation of Vote on the draft resolution on Eritrea’ article","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4ce970c5aa1b17abab413b/Eleanor_Sanders_UNHCR.png"},"location":"Geneva","political":true,"speech_type_explanation":"Transcript of the speech, exactly as it was delivered"},"document_type":"speech","first_published_at":"2026-07-07T09:51:04+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-explanation-of-vote-on-the-draft-resolution-on-eritrea","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-explanation-of-vote-on-the-draft-resolution-on-eritrea","base_path":"/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-explanation-of-vote-on-the-draft-resolution-on-eritrea","content_id":"b89c55c7-95ff-40a0-9908-6c139efcfa83","document_type":"speech","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-07T08:51:04Z","schema_name":"speech","title":"UN Human Rights Council 62: UK Explanation of Vote on the draft resolution on Eritrea","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-explanation-of-vote-on-the-draft-resolution-on-eritrea","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1315","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","base_path":"/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","content_id":"f9fcf3fe-2751-4dca-97ca-becaeceb4b26","details":{"acronym":"FCDO","brand":"foreign-commonwealth-development-office","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de4e90e0710be0354d7/s960_fcdo-main-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de48fa8f5490aff83b4/s300_fcdo-main-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Foreign, Commonwealth<br/>&amp; Development Office"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","withdrawn":false}],"people":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/eleanor-sanders","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/eleanor-sanders","base_path":"/government/people/eleanor-sanders","content_id":"4301c606-5fdc-4e77-bbf1-1dbce629f3c8","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2024-09-24T08:38:41Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Eleanor Sanders","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/eleanor-sanders","withdrawn":false}],"primary_publishing_organisation":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1315","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","base_path":"/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","content_id":"f9fcf3fe-2751-4dca-97ca-becaeceb4b26","details":{"acronym":"FCDO","brand":"foreign-commonwealth-development-office","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de4e90e0710be0354d7/s960_fcdo-main-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de48fa8f5490aff83b4/s300_fcdo-main-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Foreign, Commonwealth<br/>&amp; Development Office"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"content_id":"9066fb8d-4a60-442b-8b3f-6f6c10936714","details":{"body":"<p>The UK’s Ambassador for Human Rights exists to defend and advance human rights and democracy globally. Promoting human rights and the rule of law is fundamental to maintaining stability and preventing conflict and is therefore at the heart of the UK’s interests.  </p>\n\n<p>The Ambassador for Human Rights has 3 main objectives:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>protecting and promoting human rights within the multilateral system, including at the United Nations Human Rights Council</li>\n  <li>working in partnership with countries to support and advance human rights</li>\n  <li>promoting other human rights campaigns in support of the UK’s international priorities</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The Ambassador engages with civil society and human rights defenders. Through country missions, she engages with states, human rights institutions and other international partners to champion positive progress made by states, encourage advances and identify areas for collaboration and partnership to support protections and promotion of human rights within those countries.</p>\n","role_payment_type":null},"document_type":"ambassador_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-03-02T16:11:40Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Ambassador for Human Rights and Deputy Permanent Representative to the United Nations and other International Organisations in Geneva ","withdrawn":false}],"speaker":[{"api_p